From d172f8cbc16b0f56a85dfacf5395fd7b3ddd4567 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AK Sharma <maskachoska@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:48:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: run the AN7552 QDMA LMGR in DRAM mode

The AN7552 datapath inherits the generic QDMA LMGR init, which sets
LMGR_SRAM_MODE. On this SoC the stock firmware runs the local memory
manager in DRAM mode; with SRAM mode set the QDMA consumes TX
descriptors but never completes or transmits them, so every TX ring
wedges and no frame reaches GDM1. RX is unaffected.

Clear LMGR_SRAM_MODE for airoha_an7552 so the LMGR runs in DRAM mode,
matching stock (LMGR_INIT_CFG 0x11804000 vs 0x51804000, bit 30).

Tested on a Nokia AOT4221NK (AN7552) on top of airoha_en7552: without
this, eth0 tx_packets stays 0 and host<->board ARP never completes;
with it, ping completes with 0% loss including 1400-byte frames and the
TX queues drain.

Signed-off-by: AK Sharma <maskachoska@yahoo.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3267,11 +3267,18 @@ static int airoha_qdma_modern_init_hfwd(struct airoha_qdma *qdma)
 				   buf_size != AIROHA_MAX_PACKET_SIZE));
 	airoha_qdma_rmw(qdma, REG_FWD_DSCP_LOW_THR, FWD_DSCP_LOW_THR_MASK,
 			FIELD_PREP(FWD_DSCP_LOW_THR_MASK, 128));
+	/* The AN7552 stock firmware runs the LMGR in DRAM mode
+	 * (LMGR_SRAM_MODE clear). With SRAM mode set the QDMA consumes TX
+	 * descriptors but never completes or transmits them: the TX rings
+	 * wedge and no frame reaches GDM1. Run it in DRAM mode on AN7552.
+	 */
 	airoha_qdma_rmw(qdma, REG_LMGR_INIT_CFG,
 			LMGR_INIT_START | LMGR_SRAM_MODE_MASK |
 			HW_FWD_DESC_NUM_MASK,
 			FIELD_PREP(HW_FWD_DESC_NUM_MASK, num_desc) |
-			LMGR_INIT_START | LMGR_SRAM_MODE_MASK);
+			LMGR_INIT_START |
+			(airoha_is(qdma->eth, airoha_an7552) ? 0 :
+			 LMGR_SRAM_MODE_MASK));
 
 	return read_poll_timeout(airoha_qdma_rr, status,
 				 !(status & LMGR_INIT_START), USEC_PER_MSEC,

